  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "OAuth Mental Model and Roles",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "OAuth Mental Model and Roles",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What OAuth Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "OAuth 2.0 = ==delegated authorization==",
                "App gets **limited access** to user data, never the password",
                "OAuth answers {blue:what may this app do?}",
                "OIDC adds {green:who is the user?} on top"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Four Roles",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "cards",
              "spec": {
                "cards": [
                  {
                    "title": "Resource Owner",
                    "lines": [
                      "the user"
                    ],
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Client",
                    "lines": [
                      "the app"
                    ],
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Authorization Server",
                    "lines": [
                      "issues tokens"
                    ],
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Resource Server",
                    "lines": [
                      "API that accepts tokens"
                    ],
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Clients and Channels",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Public",
                "Confidential"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Examples",
                  "SPA, mobile",
                  "server-side app"
                ],
                [
                  "Keeps secret?",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Authenticates with",
                  "PKCE, no secret",
                  "`client_id` + `client_secret`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Front channel",
                "Back channel"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Is",
                  "browser redirects",
                  "server-to-server call"
                ],
                [
                  "Seen by",
                  "visible, ==untrusted==",
                  "hidden, ==trusted=="
                ],
                [
                  "Used for",
                  "`/authorize`",
                  "`/token`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Never put a secret in a SPA or mobile app: ==public clients cannot keep one==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Authorization Code Flow with PKCE",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Authorization Code Flow with PKCE",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Four Steps",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "1. Verifier",
                    "note": "random 43-128 chars; challenge = BASE64URL(SHA256(verifier)), method S256",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "2. /authorize",
                    "note": "response_type=code, client_id, redirect_uri, scope, state, code_challenge, code_challenge_method=S256",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "3. Callback",
                    "note": "?code=...&state=...; state must match",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "4. POST /token",
                    "note": "grant_type=authorization_code, code, redirect_uri, client_id, code_verifier",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Step 3: user logs in and consents, then the server redirects to ==redirect_uri==",
                "Step 4 is a ==back-channel== call; the server hashes the verifier and compares it to the challenge"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import base64, hashlib, secrets",
                "v = secrets.token_urlsafe(64)",
                "d = hashlib.sha256(v.encode()).digest()",
                "c = base64.urlsafe_b64encode(d).rstrip(b'=').decode()"
              ],
              "note": "S256 challenge: URL-safe base64, no = padding"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Why PKCE and Which Grant",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Grant",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Auth code + PKCE",
                  "{green:User present}, all clients"
                ],
                [
                  "`client_credentials`",
                  "Machine-to-machine, **no user**"
                ],
                [
                  "Implicit",
                  "{red:Deprecated}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "PKCE stops ==code interception==: a stolen code is useless without the verifier",
                "Use it for all clients; ==mandatory== for public clients"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Always compare ==state== on the callback. The verifier travels only on the **back channel**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Access, Refresh and ID Tokens",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Access, Refresh and ID Tokens",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Tokens",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Token",
                "Audience",
                "Lifetime",
                "Goes to"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{blue:Access}",
                  "the API",
                  "short-lived (minutes)",
                  "resource server: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`"
                ],
                [
                  "{green:ID} (OIDC JWT)",
                  "the client",
                  "short-lived (minutes); issued once at login",
                  "client only; never an API credential"
                ],
                [
                  "{orange:Refresh}",
                  "authorization server",
                  "long-lived",
                  "`/token` only; never the resource server"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Validating Tokens",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Check",
                "What it proves"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Signature via JWKS key (`kid`)",
                  "untampered"
                ],
                [
                  "`iss`",
                  "right issuer"
                ],
                [
                  "`aud`",
                  "meant for this API"
                ],
                [
                  "`exp`",
                  "not expired"
                ],
                [
                  "`nonce`",
                  "ID token only; matches the request"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Opaque tokens: ask the server through ==introspection== (RFC 7662)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Refresh and Storage",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Refresh: POST to `/token` with ==grant_type=refresh_token== for a new access token",
                "==Rotation==: every use issues a **new** refresh token",
                "Reuse of an old one is detected: revoke the token family"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "POST /token",
                "grant_type=refresh_token",
                "refresh_token=<refresh_token>",
                "client_id=<client_id>"
              ],
              "note": "back channel; no user involved"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Store in ==httpOnly secure cookies== or server-side"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Never store tokens in ==localStorage==: any XSS can read them"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Scopes, OIDC Discovery and Claims",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Scopes, OIDC Discovery and Claims",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Scopes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Scopes = permissions requested, as ==space-separated== strings: `read:calendar write:calendar`",
                "User consents; the server may ==grant less== than requested",
                "OIDC adds the ==openid== scope, required to get an ID token"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Scope",
                "Claims"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`openid`",
                  "`sub`, ID token"
                ],
                [
                  "`profile`",
                  "`name`, `picture`"
                ],
                [
                  "`email`",
                  "`email`"
                ],
                [
                  "`address` / `phone`",
                  "address / phone number"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. ID Token Claims",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Claim",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`iss`",
                  "issuer"
                ],
                [
                  "`sub`",
                  "stable unique user id"
                ],
                [
                  "`aud`",
                  "intended client"
                ],
                [
                  "`exp` / `iat`",
                  "expiry / issued at"
                ],
                [
                  "`nonce`",
                  "binds token to request"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Key on sub",
              "text": "Key users on ==sub==, never on `email`: email can change or be reused."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Discovery and userinfo",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "curl {issuer}/.well-known/openid-configuration"
              ],
              "note": "configure a client from the issuer URL alone"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Returns `authorization_endpoint`, `token_endpoint`, `userinfo_endpoint`, `jwks_uri`, supported scopes",
                "`/userinfo` returns claims for a valid ==access token==",
                "==nonce== ties the ID token to the request and stops replay"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
